content.text:
The evidence points to two root causes. The 440 ms checkout→payment gap is the main user-facing slowdown, and quote's restart is the earlier fault that spreads through shipping.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "payment",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name LIKE '%PaymentService/Charge%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "Checkout's Charge client span takes about 442 ms p50, while payment's server span stays about 1.2 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE span_name LIKE '%PaymentService/Charge%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "In the normal period checkout's Charge client span was about 2.6 ms p50 with payment at 1.2 ms."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "quote",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, count(*) n, max(value) max_restarts FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'quote%' AND metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Quote's current pod shows a restart count of 1 during the incident, versus 0 in normal; the pod is newly created."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT CAST(floor(epoch(time)/60) AS BIGINT) bucket, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'quote' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Quote's spans are sparse and slower in the first minutes of the window, then recover to lower volume."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "payment", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('checkout') AND span_name IN ('oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge','prepareOrderItemsAndShippingQuoteFromCart') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Checkout's PlaceOrder and Charge spans are slowed to hundreds of ms, while payment's own spans are unchanged."}]},
    {"from": "quote", "to": "shipping", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('quote','shipping') AND span_name IN ('POST /getquote','/get-quote','POST quote') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Quote's server p95 rises from 0.3 ms to about 4.7 ms; shipping's get-quote p95 rises from 2.4 to 9.4 ms."}]},
    {"from": "shipping", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'checkout' AND span_name = 'oteldemo.ShippingService/GetQuote' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Checkout's calls to shipping are slower and fewer in the incident window, consistent with quote's slowdown reaching checkout."}]},
    {"from": "checkout", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('frontend','checkout') GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Checkout's slowdown lines up with frontend p95 rising during the abnormal window."}]},
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend-proxy", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend-proxy' AND attr_http_response_status_code >= 500 GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend-proxy ingress returns 5xx and 504s to users, with frontend as its upstream."}]}
